  projectId?: string(name='ProjectId', description='The ID of the editing project. You can call the [CreateEditingProject](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/441137.html) operation to create an editing project and obtain the ProjectId parameter to submit an editing task.
>Notice: You must specify one of the ProjectId, Timeline, and TemplateId parameters, and leave the other two parameters empty.</notice>', example='xxxxxfb2101cb318xxxxx', position='Query'),
  projectMetadata?: string(name='ProjectMetadata', description='The metadata information of the editing project, in JSON format. For the specific structure definition, see [ProjectMetadata](~~357745#title-yvp-81k-wff~~).', example='{"Description":"Edited video description","Title":"Editing title test"}', position='Query'),
  source?: string(name='Source', description='The source of the editing and producing request. Valid values:

- OpenAPI: direct API requests.

- AliyunConsole: requests from the Alibaba Cloud Management Console.

- WebSDK: requests from frontend pages integrated with WebSDK.', example='OPENAPI', position='Query'),
  templateId?: string(name='TemplateId', description='The ID of the template. This parameter is used to quickly build a timeline with a low threshold. Video editing based on common templates and advanced templates is supported.

- When you use a template ID to submit a media editing and producing job, you must provide the ClipsParam parameter to flexibly adjust or replace materials in the template.

- You can invoke the [GetTemplate](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/441164.html) operation to obtain template information.

>Notice: You must specify one of the ProjectId, Timeline, and TemplateId parameters, and leave the other two parameters empty.', example='****96e8864746a0b6f3****', position='Query'),
  timeline?: string(name='Timeline', description='The timeline of the cloud editing task. When you need to arrange materials and design special effects based on video ideas, you can manually construct the Timeline parameter.

- A timeline mainly includes three types of objects: tracks, materials, and effects. For more information, see [Timeline configurations](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/198823.html).
- For more timeline configuration examples, see [Best practices](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/2766669.html).

>Notice: You must specify one of the ProjectId, Timeline, and TemplateId parameters, and leave the other two parameters empty.</notice>', example='{"VideoTracks":[{"VideoTrackClips":[{"MediaId":"****4d7cf14dc7b83b0e801c****"},{"MediaId":"****4d7cf14dc7b83b0e801c****"}]}]}', position='Body'),
  userData?: string(name='UserData', description='The custom settings, in JSON format. The maximum length is 512 bytes. [Task completion callback configurations](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/451631.html) are supported. Parameters:
- NotifyAddress: the callback URL for task completion.
